# Models and Core Rules

- Preserve backward compatibility: `from constrained_scheduler import ConstrainedScheduler` and `from models import ...` must remain valid.
- Changes to `core/models.py` affect schedule primitives, availability, and low-level constraints—verify `constrained_scheduler` imports still resolve.
- When changing `Activity`, `Troop`, `ScheduleEntry`, `TimeSlot`, or `Schedule`, run full unit and regression checks.
- Do not remove or rename symbols used by `core/scheduler/legacy_parts/` without updating those modules.
